<title>ITALY: Italy's Palermo sees Jan CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Palermo sees Jan CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Palermo said its January consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month on month and 1.8 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In December, Palermo's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 1.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Palermo is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.80 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.1)     1.8  (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0   (0.0)     3.3  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     2.1  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.3   (0.2)     0.4  (0.6)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0  (-0.5)     0.8  (0.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		   3.0   (0.0)     3.3  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.5   (0.1)     2.1  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1   (0.4)     0.8  (0.4)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.9)     3.0  (0.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     1.5  (1.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.1)    -0.4 (-0.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
